   $q$Which linear function passes through the points $(2, 11)$ and $(5, 20)$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$y = 3x + 11$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-y-value-as-intercept"},{"text":"$y = 3x - 5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error"},{"text":"$y = 9x - 7$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-divide-by-run"},{"text":"$y = 3x + 5$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$y = 3x + 5$$q$, $q$The slope is $\frac{20 - 11}{5 - 2} = 3$, and $11 = 3(2) + b$ gives $b = 5$, so $y = 3x + 5$. The choice $y = 3x + 11$ uses the $y$ value of the first point as the intercept even though that point is not at $x = 0$.$q$, 'draft', null)
