   $q$A museum had 200 visitors in one day: 120 adults and 80 children. Of the adults, 60 used an audio guide. Of the children, 30 used an audio guide. A visitor who used an audio guide is chosen at random. What is the probability that the visitor is a child?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{3}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{20}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-grand-total"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{8}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-the-condition"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{5}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-the-condition"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{1}{3}$$q$, $q$There are $60 + 30 = 90$ audio guide users, and 30 are children, so $P(\text{child} \mid \text{audio guide}) = \frac{30}{90} = \frac{1}{3}$. The choice $\frac{3}{8}$ is $\frac{30}{80}$, which is $P(\text{audio guide} \mid \text{child})$, the reverse condition.$q$, 'draft', null)
