  ('dc17bb25-5cdc-52fa-9f38-2c5432e81414', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'math-g10-conditional-probability'), null, 'medium',
   $q$For events $A$ and $B$, $P(A) = 0.45$, $P(B) = 0.35$, and $P(A \text{ or } B) = 0.6$. What is $P(A \text{ and } B)$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0.2$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$0.8$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-the-events"},{"text":"$0.1575$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-independence"},{"text":"$0.4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-p-of-neither"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$0.2$$q$, $q$Rearrange the addition rule: $P(A \text{ and } B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \text{ or } B) = 0.45 + 0.35 - 0.6 = 0.2$. The choice $0.1575$ multiplies $0.45 \cdot 0.35$, which is only valid if the events are known to be independent.$q$, 'draft', null)
