   $q$Events $A$ and $B$ are independent. If $P(A) = 0.4$ and $P(A \text{ and } B) = 0.12$, what is $P(B)$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0.3$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$0.28$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-instead-of-divided"},{"text":"$0.048$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"multiplied-instead-of-divided"},{"text":"$0.52$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-instead-of-divided"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$0.3$$q$, $q$Independence gives $P(A) \cdot P(B) = P(A \text{ and } B)$, so $0.4 \cdot P(B) = 0.12$ and $P(B) = \frac{0.12}{0.4} = 0.3$. The choice $0.048$ multiplies $0.4 \cdot 0.12$ instead of dividing.$q$, 'draft', null)
