   $q$A science fair had 60 projects: 24 in biology and 36 in physics. Of the biology projects, 18 won a ribbon. Of the physics projects, 12 won a ribbon. A project that won a ribbon is chosen at random. What is the probability that it is a biology project?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{3}{10}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-grand-total"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{5}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-the-condition"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-the-condition"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{5}$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{3}{5}$$q$, $q$There are $18 + 12 = 30$ ribbon winners, and 18 are biology projects, so $P(\text{biology} \mid \text{ribbon}) = \frac{18}{30} = \frac{3}{5}$. The choice $\frac{3}{4}$ is $\frac{18}{24}$, the probability a biology project won a ribbon, which reverses the condition.$q$, 'draft', null)
