   $q$At a community garden, 60 percent of volunteers arrive in the morning and the rest arrive in the afternoon. Of the morning volunteers, $0.5$ bring their own tools. Of the afternoon volunteers, $0.25$ bring their own tools. What is the probability that a randomly chosen volunteer brings their own tools?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0.75$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-the-conditionals"},{"text":"$0.4$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$0.375$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"averaged-the-conditionals"},{"text":"$0.3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-the-afternoon-group"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$0.4$$q$, $q$Add the two joint probabilities: $0.6 \cdot 0.5 + 0.4 \cdot 0.25 = 0.3 + 0.1 = 0.4$. The choice $0.375$ averages $0.5$ and $0.25$, which ignores that the morning group is larger than the afternoon group.$q$, 'draft', null)
