   $q$A weather station finds that 40 percent of days are cloudy. On cloudy days, the probability of rain is $0.75$. On days that are not cloudy, the probability of rain is $0.25$. Given that it rained on a randomly chosen day, what is the probability that the day was cloudy?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{2}{3}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{10}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-joint-probability"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-the-condition"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{5}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-the-new-information"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{2}{3}$$q$, $q$$P(\text{cloudy and rain}) = 0.4 \cdot 0.75 = 0.3$ and $P(\text{rain}) = 0.3 + 0.6 \cdot 0.25 = 0.45$, so $P(\text{cloudy} \mid \text{rain}) = \frac{0.3}{0.45} = \frac{2}{3}$. The choice $\frac{3}{4}$ is $P(\text{rain} \mid \text{cloudy})$, the reverse condition.$q$, 'draft', null)
