   $q$Ravi constructs the perpendicular bisector of $\overline{AB}$ and picks a point $P$ on it. Ravi finds $PA = 3x + 2$ and $PB = 5x - 6$. What is $PA$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$14$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$28$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-both-distances"},{"text":"$4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stopped-at-x"},{"text":"$7$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"halved-the-distance"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$14$$q$, $q$Every point on the perpendicular bisector is equally far from $A$ and $B$, so $3x + 2 = 5x - 6$, giving $x = 4$ and $PA = 3(4) + 2 = 14$. The choice $4$ is the value of $x$, not the distance.$q$, 'draft', null)
