  ('3ef6cc4f-c802-5390-861c-2b5c1ea40aa2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'math-g10-constructions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Through point $P$ not on line $\ell$, Hiroshi constructs line $m$ perpendicular to $\ell$. Hiroshi then constructs line $n$ through $P$ perpendicular to $m$. How is line $n$ related to line $\ell$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$n$ is the same line as $m$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-the-two-lines"},{"text":"$n$ meets $\\ell$ at a $45^\\circ$ angle","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"averaged-the-angles"},{"text":"$n$ is parallel to $\\ell$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$n$ is perpendicular to $\\ell$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thinks-two-perpendiculars-give-perpendicular"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$n$ is parallel to $\ell$$q$, $q$Lines $n$ and $\ell$ are both perpendicular to $m$, and two lines perpendicular to the same line in a plane are parallel. Turning $90^\circ$ twice brings the direction back to that of $\ell$, not perpendicular to it.$q$, 'draft', null)
