   $q$Bao tries to copy a $37^\circ$ angle $\angle ABC$. Bao draws an arc centered at $B$ crossing the sides at $D$ and $F$, and an arc with the same width centered at $E$ crossing the new ray at $G$. By mistake Bao then keeps the compass at width $BD$, draws an arc centered at $G$ that meets the first arc at $H$, and draws ray $EH$. What is the measure of $\angle GEH$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$90^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-right-angle"},{"text":"$74^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"doubled-the-angle"},{"text":"$37^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thinks-copy-still-correct"},{"text":"$60^\\circ$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$60^\circ$$q$, $q$Now $EG = EH = GH = BD$, so triangle $EGH$ is equilateral and $\angle GEH = 60^\circ$ no matter what angle Bao started with. The choice $37^\circ$ assumes the copy still works, but the copy needs the chord $DF$, not the radius.$q$, 'draft', null)
