   $q$Nia designs a logo by inscribing an equilateral triangle in a circle of radius $10$ cm with a compass and straightedge. To the nearest tenth of a centimeter, what is the perimeter of the triangle?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$42.4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-square-rule"},{"text":"$52.0$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$60.0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-diameter-as-side"},{"text":"$30.0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-hexagon-rule"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$52.0$$q$, $q$Each side of an equilateral triangle inscribed in a circle of radius $r$ is $r\sqrt{3}$, so the perimeter is $3 \cdot 10\sqrt{3} = 30\sqrt{3} \approx 51.96$, which rounds to $52.0$. The choice $30.0$ uses side length $10$, which is the side of the inscribed hexagon.$q$, 'draft', null)
